  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At 3% a year, $100 buys about $74 of today's goods in 10 years (100/1.03^10 = 74.4) and about $55 in 20 years (55.4). Calculo proprio.",
      "status": "cited",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.bls.gov/data/inflation_calculator.htm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At 3% inflation, $10,000 in cash buys what $7,441 buys today after 10 years. Calculo proprio.",
      "status": "cited",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.bls.gov/data/inflation_calculator.htm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "By the Rule of 72, 72 divided by 3 is 24: at 3% a year, prices double, and cash loses half its buying power, in about 24 years.",
      "status": "cited",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/glossary/rule-72"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The BLS CPI Inflation Calculator compares the buying power of a dollar between two dates.",
